### Ask a question + give feedback (QuestionController, /rest/v1)
### No auth required - /rest/** is permitAll (see ResourceServerConfig).
###
### Each "Ask ..." request stores the question and returns a questionId.
### Its response handler saves conversationId/questionId as GLOBAL variables
### (client.global), so http/sse/sse.http can pick them up and run the rest
### of the flow (subscribe -> trigger processing -> feedback) against the
### same question. Run ONE of the three "Ask ..." requests below, then
### switch to sse.http.

### 1. Ask a question routed to HELLO_AGENT (greeting / off-topic / "what can you do")
@newConversationId = {{$uuid}}

POST {{host}}/rest/v1/question?conversationId={{newConversationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Hi! What can you help me with?"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("conversationId", response.body.conversationId);
    client.global.set("questionId", response.body.questionId);
%}

###

### 2. Ask a question routed to DOCUMENT_AGENT (content lookup inside uploaded documents)
@newConversationId = {{$uuid}}

POST {{host}}/rest/v1/question?conversationId={{newConversationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "What does the onboarding document say about the approval process?"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("conversationId", response.body.conversationId);
    client.global.set("questionId", response.body.questionId);
%}

###

### 3. Ask a question routed to QUESTION_SQL_AGENT (lookup in the TI Knowledge DB)
@newConversationId = {{$uuid}}

POST {{host}}/rest/v1/question?conversationId={{newConversationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Show me interview questions about Java concurrency stored in the knowledge base."
}

> {%
    client.global.set("conversationId", response.body.conversationId);
    client.global.set("questionId", response.body.questionId);
%}

###

### 4. Submit feedback for the last question captured above (run after sse.http's
### "trigger processing" request has produced an answer). Uses the GLOBAL
### conversationId/questionId saved by whichever "Ask ..." request you ran.
POST {{host}}/rest/v1/feedback?conversationId={{conversationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "questionId": {{questionId}},
  "feedback": "This answer was helpful."
}

###
